course: dictionary
lesson: 6841
title: Outline: shape and plan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An outline is the edge of something, the line that shows its shape. «A shadow shows the outline of the thing in the way.» The shadow is dark inside, but its edge is the shape of the object that blocks the light.
explain: Outline can also mean a short plan. It gives the main points and leaves out the details. Before you write a story, you can write an outline: the main events in order, one line each.
explain: As a verb, to outline means to explain the main points, or to draw the edge of something. «Outline the main points» means tell the big ideas, not every detail. Context tells you which meaning fits: a shape, a plan, or an action.
fact: An outline is a line that shows the shape or edge of something.
fact: An outline is also a short plan with the main points, not all the details.
fact: «Outline» can be a verb: to outline a plan is to explain its main points.
fact: «In outline» means in a short, simple form, with only the main parts.
fact: «Stripes break up the tiger's outline», which helps it hide in the grass.
exercise: «A shadow shows the outline of the thing in the way.» In this sentence, what is an outline? | *The edge or shape of the thing | A loud noise | A plan for a story | A dark colour inside a room
exercise: Ms Lee asks for an outline of your story before you write. What does she want? | A list of your favourite colours | *The main points, in a short plan | A drawing of the castle | Every word of the story
exercise: In art, pupils draw the outline first and then colour in. What is the outline? | *The first lines that show the shape, before colouring | The frame around the picture | The final colours on the picture | The paper the picture is drawn on
test: «The okapi's stripy legs break up its outline in the shadows.» What does this help the okapi do? | Run much faster | Find more food | Grow taller | *Be hard to see
test: Priya must outline the main points of a book report. What should she write? | A poem about the book | Only the title of the book | *A short plan with the main points | Every page copied out
exam: In which sentence does outline mean a plan? | Stripes break up the tiger's outline | The lamp made a bright patch on the wall | *Her outline had three main points | The outline of the tree was black against the sky
